# Bash Quality Rules

## Syntax Requirements
- Must pass `bash -n` syntax check
- No syntax errors allowed

## Header Requirements
- Must have shebang: #!/bin/bash or #!/bin/sh
- Should include brief description comment

## Error Handling
- Use `set -e` or explicit error handling
- Check return codes for important operations
- Use trap for cleanup

## Variable Usage
- Quote all variables: "$VAR" not $VAR
- Use local in functions
- Avoid global variables when possible
- No hardcoded paths (use variables)

## Code Style
- Maximum line length: 100 characters
- Use meaningful variable names
- Functions should have comments
- Use indentation consistently

## Best Practices
- Use [[ ]] for tests, not [ ]
- Use $() instead of backticks
- Prefer printf over echo for formatting
- Check if commands exist before using

## Scoring
- Missing shebang: -10 points
- No error handling: -5 points
- Unquoted variables: -1 point each (max -10)
- Line too long: -1 point per line
- Syntax error: -30 points (critical)
